  "id": "COMPOUND:1727 - PROTEIN:5848",
  "verbalization": "Castanospermine is implicated in the relationship with Raji through a multi-step pathway involving a sialyltransferase enzyme. The enzyme, CMP-N-acetylneuraminate-beta-1,4-galactoside alpha-2,3-sialyltransferase, is identified as a target of multiple compounds, including (3aR,6S,6aR)-3,6-bis(3,4,5-trimethoxyphenyl)-1,3,3a,4,6,6a-hexahydrofuro[3,4-c]furan and 6'-O-Z-Para-Methoxycinnamoylharpagide. These compounds are linked to Raji through their target enzyme, suggesting a potential mechanism of action involving the sialyltransferase. The presence of multiple pathways converging on the same target enzyme supports a role for Castanospermine in modulating Raji cell activity through this enzyme. The integration of these pathways highlights the enzyme as a central mediator in the interaction between Castanospermine and Raji, emphasizing its importance in the biological process.",
